The top decile is the regime where the model's assumption holds, and there it does exactly what you described: 繁星's two bars together select students about 5 ability points above what the 學測 cutoff alone implies. Below that it overshoots badly, and the reason is structural rather than a tuning problem. I compute the mean ability of everyone the bars make eligible nationally. A competitive department really does draw from that whole pool. A department in the 20–29 decile does not — only weak schools apply to it, so its admits are the bottom of the eligible pool, not its average.  Nothing in the data says which schools apply where
